      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Anglin’s Fishing Pier honors Lauderdale‑by‑the‑Sea’s first mayor, Melvin I., and sits at the ocean’s edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauderdale-by-the-Sea%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "unverified=['smith']"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2016, the town earned the title Florida’s Beach Diving Capital thanks to a coral reef just 100 yards offshore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauderdale-by-the-Sea%2C_Florida",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2013 streetscape overhaul widened sidewalks, added brick pavers, and installed coral‑reef themed artworks across four commercial plazas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauderdale-by-the-Sea%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town stretches half a dozen blocks on a narrow barrier island, separated from the mainland by the Intracoastal Waterway and a single drawbridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauderdale-by-the-Sea%2C_Florida",
